::  name       mantra line field count
::  shape      fields - int (@u32)
::  invariant  a weave Line carries exactly five fields (text - gen - pos - site - run)
::  example    5
::  readers    Mantra - Glow Tend - Sur museum - Ashvini nest-only
::  nib        equinox-e203-mantra-tend-v0
::
::  Equinox e203 - Mantra M1 -- first Mantra structure pedestal in src/shape/.
::  Names Line's field count from mantra/src/weave.rye. Pedestal only; Rye
::  still owns Weave - Diff - apply - current.
::
::  Moved three to four on 20260906.212206, when `site` landed beside `pos`.
::  A position counter runs inside one weave, so two weaves that parted hand
::  the same small integer to different lines; the site is what makes the pair
::  unique, and it is why two branches can merge at all. REDS %500 is the row
::  that made this placard COUNT rather than grep for presence -- a fourth
::  field used to pass it -- so this refusal on the lap the fourth field
::  arrived is that row's own instrument working.
::
::  Moved four to five on 20260907.173200, when document order left `LineId`
::  for `Place`. A line now carries the run that placed it, so every line of
::  one `apply` sorts as one block and two branches each appending a paragraph
::  come back whole rather than alternating. The count refused on that lap
::  too, which is the same instrument working a second time.
+$  mantra-line-field-count-shape
  $:  fields=@u32
  ==
